ief priests and scribes stood there, vehemently accusing Him.","23:11":"And even Herod and his soldiers ridiculed and mocked Him. Dressing Him in a fine robe, they sent Him back to Pilate.","23:12":"That day Herod and Pilate became friends; before this time they had been enemies.","23:13":"Then Pilate called together the chief priests, the rulers, and the people,","23:14":"and said to them, “You brought me this man as one who was inciting the people to rebellion. I have examined Him here in your presence and found Him not guilty of your charges against Him.","23:15":"Neither has Herod, for he sent Him back to us. As you can see, He has done nothing deserving of death.","23:16":"Therefore I will punish Him and release Him.”"}}},"pairs":{},"minor":[]}